## `#NodeConfig`

`kind.control_plane` and each `workers` value take node settings. The `kind` driver accepts kind's [per-node options](https://kind.sigs.k8s.io/docs/user/configuration/#per-node-options), with kind's field names. The `k3d` driver accepts none, so write each `workers` value as `{}`. For example, with `kind`:

```cue
cluster: {
    uses: "builtin:kubernetes"
    with: {
        driver: "kind"
        kind: control_plane: extraMounts: [{hostPath: "./src", containerPath: "/workspace"}]
        workers: worker_a: image: "kindest/node:v1.34.0"
    }
}
```

kevin merges these with its own node settings:

- `labels` adds to the `kevin.node` label. You cannot set `kevin.node`.
- `extraPortMappings` adds to the relay port mapping.
- You cannot set `role`.

The control-plane node has the label `kevin.node: control-plane`.

